    "text": {
     "en": "Science grows through observation, questions, experiments and new ideas. Old ideas are tested and sometimes replaced when better evidence appears.\nIndian scientists such as C. V. Raman, Jagadish Chandra Bose and Aryabhata made important discoveries.\nScientific thinking means asking questions, collecting evidence and not accepting a claim without proof."
